# files; the 30 worst files, guava's own collection implementations, hold 55% of them), 247 to class files. Without
# verdicts (maddi-run-openjdk's guava.ratchet, recorded at an older maddi) 355 files compile.
# 2026-10-16, devel at maddi 522dc2f2f / maddi-mod f5d1bf79: the printer's guava work of the day (an enclosing type's
# type variable in concrete supertypes, Kotlin's signatures for mapped collection and Map-default overrides, fields
# renamed off mapped properties, java.lang.reflect.Array qualified, inner classes of generic classes by simple name,
# class headers qualifying their own nested types, abstract equals/hashCode left out of interfaces, …) and
# maddi-null's override-family, test-override, bounded-slot and type-variable-slot verdicts (maddi-mod#50 follow-ups):
# 389 files compiling (1,342 type errors), 280 to class files, 246 test files to class files; syntax-clean, all 610.
